<%# THE BUTTON THAT SPLITS THE PAYCHECK — the one control in this app that moves money between
    pools. Locals: `presenter` (DistributionPresenter), `standalone` (boolean).

    Two shapes, one label, because the screen has two densities (spec §5) and the button belongs
    to both: the all-clear screen is "headline, one summary line, one button", and the waterfall
    puts it beside the recompute. The copy lives here once so the two cannot drift.

    THE EXPANDED SHAPE IS A SUBMITTER INSIDE THE WATERFALL'S OWN FORM, and that is the whole
    point of it. The boxes are that form's fields, so confirming submits WHAT THE USER HAS
    TYPED — including an edit they never pressed "Update figures" on. A separate form carrying
    the already-applied overrides as hidden fields would have been simpler and would silently
    write $500 into an envelope the user had just typed 200 into, which is the screen and the
    ledger disagreeing about money on the one screen where that is unforgivable. The form itself
    stays a GET to `new` (its `method`/`action` are unchanged); `formaction` and `formmethod`
    move only THIS button's submission.

    THE TOKEN RIDES ON THE BUTTON, not in a hidden field, and the reason is the same GET form: a
    hidden `authenticity_token` would be serialised into the query string every time someone
    pressed "Update figures", putting the session's CSRF token in the URL bar, the browser
    history and the server log. A submit button's own name/value pair is submitted only when
    that button is the one clicked, so the token exists for the POST and for nothing else.
    Turbo also sends the token as a header, so this is what keeps the POST working with
    JavaScript off rather than the only guard. %>
<% if standalone %>
  <%= form_with url: distributions_path, method: :post do %>
    <%# Without this the write falls back to "the account the pay landed in", which is a
        different account the moment a second paycheck arrives mid-period. %>
    <%= hidden_field_tag :account_id, presenter.account.id %>
    <button type="submit" class="btn btn-primary" id="confirm-distribution">Confirm distribution</button>
  <% end %>
<% else %>
  <button type="submit"
          class="btn btn-primary"
          id="confirm-distribution"
          formaction="<%= distributions_path %>"
          formmethod="post"
          name="authenticity_token"
          value="<%= form_authenticity_token %>">
    Confirm distribution
  </button>
<% end %>
